ependent journalists like hopewell  chinono  have been arrested after running stories  on alleged government corruption  amucheawa says his captors wanted  information on his  uncle mudaduzi matutu he's the editor  of the zim live news site and currently  in hiding  they wanted to know about him and they  wanted to know his sources of  information where does he get  information  where does his newspaper get his funding  through him they were saying i  he had been also recruited to  become part of the cia you know it was  so ridiculous  [Music]  the university student says he was  driven to a clearing  outside the city it marked the beginning  he alleges  of three days of mental and physical  torture  i got off the car  then they said kneel down  then they said kneel down and  one of the guys pointed an ak-47  in my head then they said  make your last prayer  say your last words before we kill you  you know i  it's okay take your time take your time  yeah  and i accepted my own death i was really  convinced that  i was not going to die then one of the  guys then said  after my my long prayer rather  he then said we are not going to kill  you now  we must torture you first  [Music]  machewa claims he was strung up on a  v-shaped tree  and his back and buttocks were flailed  with sticks  when he was untied he says his captors  proceeded  to sexually humiliate him  they then did something which  i still sometimes not  comfortable to talk about you know  sometimes you are the one who is abused  and  at the end of the day you are the one we  have to  live with the shame  he was taken to a farmhouse where the  interrogation  and the interrogation techniques  continued  but he claims a number of his captors  wanted to speed things up  at some point they received a call i  believe it was from one of their bosses  and they are discussing and they are  saying oh tawanda is only 22 years old  we should get rid of him just imagine if  he  get to 30 he will give us a lot of  problems so we should just get rid of  him  now and forever this document  may have saved the student's life it's a  court order  obtained by this human rights lawyer  requiring the zimbabwean police to find  machiawa  and present him in court within 72 hours  with as much as we knew that has been  taken by the police and state security  agents  they you know they pretended to  have no knowledge about it you know and  we knew that something was alright  they have to be compelled by a  hypothetical to bring  back to them unfortunately they did so  the 22 year old says he was loaded into  a car  and driven back to bulawayo when the  vehicle was stopped at police  checkpoints  machewa says his captors identified  themselves  as ferrets the name of a shadowy police  unit  that's been implicated in civilian  abductions  when you go to police checkpoints you  you you think  maybe this is where i'm going to watch  to get help  but you know these people they just say  ferret  and they pass at some points they would  harass the police harass the soldiers  and in the road and you know  you would wonder you know who are these  people with so much power  he says they dumped him on the outskirts  of the city and issued a series of  threats  tell people what happened or seek  treatment at a hospital  and will kill you but the 22 year old  didn't have a choice  his body was battered and hospital  records show  his kidneys were barely functioning what  happened to me in weeds i feel sometimes  is doing injustice  you know the pain was just so intense  and i you know you know  you would just be wishing that it was  better if i had  died or you know  the issue is clearly sensitive for the  zimbabwean government  this student leader in red was beaten  and arrested  when he held a meeting in support of the  22 year old student  the authorities did not respond to our  inquiries  although they have accused people of  faking abductions in return for western  funds in the past  no it's not the